"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and April to May came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025, July to August and August to September each came in at 78% of normal, and November to December at 61%. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 36% of normal and May to June at 175%. Grid 21775 had its driest year in 1963 at 64% of normal.</p>"}
